{"term":"evaporate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:16813c728892645120","definition":"To transition from a liquid state into a gaseous state.","example":"When an ultrasonic beam is fired at the microcannons, the emulsion evaporates, expanding rapidly into gas. This creates enough force to push the nanobullets out at velocities reaching several metres per second.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ergative","register":"ergative","wordFamily":["coevaporate","evaporative","nonevaporated","nonevaporating","photoevaporate","reevaporate","unevaporated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evaporate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:989bc90fa253a07179","definition":"To expel moisture from (usually by means of artificial heat), leaving the solid portion.","example":"to evaporate apples","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coevaporate","evaporative","nonevaporated","nonevaporating","photoevaporate","reevaporate","unevaporated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evaporate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f529ca7406627476c2","definition":"To give vent to; to dissipate.","example":"[M]y lord of Eſſex choſe to evaporate his thoughts in a Sonnet (being his common vvay) to be ſung before the Queen, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["coevaporate","evaporative","nonevaporated","nonevaporating","photoevaporate","reevaporate","unevaporated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evaporate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:517b8ee3373422537e",